\section{Outlet elevation convention}{

\code{elev} is always given as an absolute elevation on the hypsography /
\verb{&morphometry} \code{H} datum. For a fixed outlet it is written straight to
\code{outl_elvs} (GLM requires \verb{base_elev <= elev <= crest_elev}). For a floating
offtake GLM instead wants a depth \emph{below the moving surface}, so \code{elev} is
converted with \code{surface_elev - elev} and must satisfy
\verb{0 <= surface_elev - elev <= (crest_elev - base_elev)}.
}

